  "content": "![The OpenAI logo is displayed on a cell phone in front of an image generated by ChatGPT's Dall-E text-to-image model, Dec. 8, 2023, in Boston. (AP Photo/Michael Dwyer, File)](https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/4258b74/2147483647/strip/true/crop/4000x2667+0+0/resize/319x213!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F9d%2F65%2Fe3f026e925f279d29de9ab26374e%2Fbb07084d1ba54a11b3a7f1a021cb7a85)\n\nThe OpenAI logo is displayed on a cell phone in front of an image generated by ChatGPT’s Dall-E text-to-image model, Dec. 8, 2023, in Boston. (AP Photo/Michael Dwyer, File)\n\n[License this photo](https://newsroom.ap.org/editorial-photos-videos/detail?mediatype=photo&utm_source=apnews&utm_campaign=gallery&itemid=bb07084d1ba54a11b3a7f1a021cb7a85)\n\n  [![](https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/7690d78/2147483647/strip/true/crop/3692x3692+1548+0/resize/60x60!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F31%2Fd6%2F348dde6a477e937d099b4e5f18bc%2F20180427-dcda102.JPG)](https://apnews.com/author/thomas-beaumont)\n\nBy  [THOMAS BEAUMONT](https://apnews.com/author/thomas-beaumont)\n\nUpdated 10:45 PM GMT-3, September 28, 2026\n\n[Leer en español](https://apnews.com/article/openai-altman-trump-astra-ia-9f0d2d6be3d3cb8a3cafe7d4eef32584)\n\n![Comments](https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/4f4506e/2147483647/strip/true/crop/112x119+0+0/resize/112x119!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F8c%2F0d%2F15433a314663a3ae8a349ee0d9fa%2Fveifora-comment-icon.png)\n\nShare\n\n-   [\n\n    Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/dialog/share?app_id=870613919693099&display=popup&href=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Fopen-ai-artificial-intelligence-altman-trump-astra-5afb865b2cddc439efdcf31ebdc406a5%3Futm_source%3DFacebook%26utm_medium%3Dshare)\n-   Copy\n\n    Link copied\n\n-   Print\n-   [\n\n    Email](mailto:?body=OpenAI%20delays%20latest%20model%20over%20security%20concerns%2C%20as%20industry%20faces%20new%20safety%20pressures%0A%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Fopen-ai-artificial-intelligence-altman-trump-astra-5afb865b2cddc439efdcf31ebdc406a5%3Futm_source%3DEmail%26utm_medium%3Dshare%0A%0AOpenAI%20says%20it%20is%20delaying%20the%20release%20of%20a%20new%20artificial%20intelligence%20model%20out%20of%20security%20concerns%20voiced%20by%20its%20researchers%2C%20the%20latest%20in%20the%20company%E2%80%99s%20effort%20to%20decelerate%20the%20pace%20of%20the%20technology%E2%80%99s%20advance.)\n-   [\n\n    X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Fopen-ai-artificial-intelligence-altman-trump-astra-5afb865b2cddc439efdcf31ebdc406a5%3Futm_source%3Dtwitter%26utm_medium%3Dshare&text=OpenAI%20delays%20latest%20model%20over%20security%20concerns%2C%20as%20industry%20faces%20new%20safety%20pressures)\n-   [\n\n    LinkedIn](#)\n-   [\n\n    Bluesky](https://bsky.app/intent/compose?text=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Fopen-ai-artificial-intelligence-altman-trump-astra-5afb865b2cddc439efdcf31ebdc406a5%3Futm_source%3Dbluesky%26utm_medium%3Dshare%26nbsp%3B%3Cbr%3EOpenAI%20delays%20latest%20model%20over%20security%20concerns%2C%20as%20industry%20faces%20new%20safety%20pressures)\n-   [\n\n    Flipboard](https://share.flipboard.com/bookmarklet/popout?v=2&title=OpenAI%20delays%20latest%20model%20over%20security%20concerns%2C%20as%20industry%20faces%20new%20safety%20pressures&url=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Fopen-ai-artificial-intelligence-altman-trump-astra-5afb865b2cddc439efdcf31ebdc406a5%3Futm_source%3DFlipboard%20Share%26utm_medium%3Dshare)\n-   [\n\n    Pinterest](https://pinterest.com/pin/create/bookmarklet/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Fopen-ai-artificial-intelligence-altman-trump-astra-5afb865b2cddc439efdcf31ebdc406a5%3Futm_source%3DPinterest%26utm_medium%3Dshare&description=OpenAI%20delays%20latest%20model%20over%20security%20concerns%2C%20as%20industry%20faces%20new%20safety%20pressures&media=https://assets.apnews.com/9d/65/e3f026e925f279d29de9ab26374e/bb07084d1ba54a11b3a7f1a021cb7a85)\n-   [\n\n    Reddit](<https://www.reddit.com/submit?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Fopen-ai-artificial-intelligence-altman-trump-astra-5afb865b2cddc439efdcf31ebdc406a5%3Futm_source%3Dreddit%26utm_medium%3Dshare&title=Reddit Share>)\n\nOpenAI said Monday it was delaying the release of a new [artificial intelligence](https://apnews.com/hub/artificial-intelligence) model out of security concerns voiced by its researchers, the latest in the company’s effort to decelerate the pace of the technology’s advance.\n\nOpenAI’s decision to hold back the model, called GPT-6.1 Astra, comes amid a broader push within the industry to slow the development of increasingly autonomous systems until safety measures can catch up. The announcement comes a day before AI executives are set to huddle with President [Donald Trump](https://apnews.com/hub/donald-trump) in Washington as technology companies face new pressure to be accountable for how their models can be abused.\n\nThe Wall Street Journal was first to report the delay of OpenAI’s model release.\n\nIn a statement from OpenAI’s head of safety systems Saachi Jain, the version “didn’t quite meet the bar.” It had become more persistent in completing tasks, but OpenAI needed to balance that capability against unauthorized behavior.\n\nJain insisted the company was committed to ensuring the model was safe whether in the company’s testing or is in the hands of users. “We have an extremely high bar in terms of safety and alignment,” she said.\n\nOpenAI paused training of its most advanced models last week, saying training would resume “only when we are confident that we have additional safeguards.”\n\nRelated Stories\n\nThat was after it disclosed instances in which AI agents exceeded their instructions, including by accessing government websites without authorization.\n\nOpenAI CEO Sam Altman has joined other industry leaders in calling for a slowdown, warning that companies do not yet have adequate safeguards to control the most capable systems. Altman was scheduled to deliver the keynote address for OpenAI’s annual conference for software developers on Tuesday in San Francisco. OpenAI President Greg Brockman is expected to attend the White House’s event Tuesday.\n\n  [![THOMAS BEAUMONT](https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/32dd3e4/2147483647/strip/true/crop/3692x3692+1548+0/resize/100x100!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F31%2Fd6%2F348dde6a477e937d099b4e5f18bc%2F20180427-dcda102.JPG)](https://apnews.com/author/thomas-beaumont)\n\n[THOMAS BEAUMONT](https://apnews.com/author/thomas-beaumont)\n\nBeaumont covers national politics for The Associated Press. He is based in Des Moines, Iowa.\n\n[\n\ntwitter](https://twitter.com/TomBeaumont)[\n\nmailto](mailto:TBeaumont@ap.org)"
